<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`liftPair`).** The product lift of consistent sets $u$ and $v$ is the finite union of the left lift of $u$ with the right lift of $v$.

**Theorem (`ProdCon_liftPair`).** The product lift of two consistent sets is product-consistent.

*Proof.* Left and right projections of the lift reduce to the given consistent sets (up to bottoms). □

**Theorem (`fstFinset_liftPair`).** The first projection of a product lift is the first set united with the first projection of the right lift.

*Proof.* Expand the lift as a finite union and apply first-projection lemmas. □

**Theorem (`sndFinset_liftPair`).** The second projection of a product lift is the second projection of the left lift united with the second set.

*Proof.* Expand the lift as a finite union and apply second-projection lemmas. □

**Theorem (`entSet_liftPair`).** Product entailment of a lift follows from factor entailments of its components.

*Proof.* Lift the two entailments through the left and right embeddings and unite. □

**Theorem (`liftLeft_funion`).** Left lift preserves finite unions.

*Proof.* Compare membership on both sides. □

**Theorem (`liftRight_funion`).** Right lift preserves finite unions.

*Proof.* Compare membership on both sides. □
